# NinjaOne

## What is NinjaOne

NinjaOne is a unified IT operations platform built for Enterprise IT Teams and MSPs to simplify IT work by unifying endpoint management, automation, and security together in one platform. NinjaOne began as an attempt to modernize remote monitoring and management (RMM) software for managed service providers (MSPs). Co‑founders Sal Sferlazza and Chris Materese launched the company (then “NinjaRMM”) in 2013 and released its platform publicly in 2015. The company’s mission is to simplify IT management by delivering a cloud‑native platform that centralizes visibility, security, and control over endpoints, servers, and SaaS applications. It rebranded to NinjaOne to reflect a broader focus on unified endpoint management across internal IT teams and MSPs. The organization has grown rapidly: by 2025 it surpassed 30,000 customers and 2,000 employees, managing over 5 million endpoints. After raising a $231.5M Series C round in 2024 led by ICONIQ Growth and a $500M series C extension in 2025 led by ICONIQ Growth and CapitalG, Alphabet’s independent investment fund (bringing its valuation to $5B), NinjaOne expanded its product suite and global presence. In mid‑2025 it acquired backup provider Dropsuite for $270M to offer unified backup across endpoints, servers and SaaS tools. In 2025, NinjaOne surpassed $500 Million in ARR in Record Fiscal Year. In June 2026, NinjaOne announced a $12.3 billion valuation following more than $400 million in Series C extensions. The extensions included participation from Wellington Management, Teachers’ Venture Growth (TVG), BDT & MSD Partners’ affiliated funds, Sequoia Capital, ICONIQ, Hedosophia, NEA, Washington Harbour Partners, CapitalG, and Pinegrove Opportunity Partners. The company remains founder-led and debt-free, with co-founders Sal Sferlazza and Chris Matarese retaining majority control.




